    "description": "Compiler developer for HPE/Cray's supercomputer compiler, which is based on the open-source LLVM compiler toolkit project.  My first project was to use GIT wizardry to bring Cray's compiler up-to-date with upstream LLVM.  Both Cray's compiler and upstream LLVM are large projects, each containing thousands of files and hundreds of thousands of lines of code. Cray's compiler had fallen three years behind upstream at the time of my hiring, and is now up-to-date.  As a result of my efforts, HPE/Cray's compiler now leverages the latest features and enhancements from the upstream community, and HPE is no longer expending resources to fix bugs that had already been fixed upstream.\n\nSince finishing that work, I have been improving the debugging experience with the HPE/Cray compiler.  I’ve brought the Fortran compiler up to DWARF 5 compatibility, and I’ve improved the GPU debugging experience in Fortran as well.",
